  "body": "## What (plan \u00a73.4/\u00a73.5, PR 8)\n- `src/prs.rs`: `slug_from_origin` (ssh, ssh://, https, and the `github-neverhuman:` alias forms \u2192 `owner/name`), `repos_from_board` (active claims \u222a last-7-day entries \u222a cwd; origin via the crate's git wrapper), `list` (`gh pr list -R <slug> --state open --limit 50 --json \u2026`, `GH_PROMPT_DISABLED=1`, `NO_COLOR=1`, 10 s timeout with kill; per-repo failures skipped, total failure \u2192 `gh unavailable: \u2026`, exit 1), tolerant `Value \u2192 Pr`, and `plain_table`.\n- `missing` per PR, in order: `CI: n failing` / `CI: n pending` / `review: no REVIEW: approve <head-sha> comment` / `mergeStateStatus: X` / `draft`; an empty list renders `-> ready`. `NEUTRAL`/`SKIPPED` count as passing (GitHub semantics), `ACTION_REQUIRED`/`STARTUP_FAILURE`/`STALE` as failing.\n- `src/main.rs`: only the `Prs` arm (`repos_from_board(&dir.join(\"bf.sqlite\"))` \u2192 table).\n- `tests/bin/gh` (mode 755) + `tests/fixtures/prs/neverhuman__fixture-a.json`: shim answering only `gh pr list -R <slug> \u2026`; `tests/cli_prs.rs` (5): board-derived repos through the shim, cwd-only, `gh` missing \u2192 exit 1, slug mapping, `missing` derivation. `tests/cli_skeleton.rs`: `prs` leaves the exit-3 list.\n\n## Evidence\nIsolated tree on current main: fmt/clippy `-D warnings` clean; all test binaries green; `bash scripts/check` EXIT 0 in 15 s. Real run on this host (`bf prs` from the bf checkout, 0.84 s): listed `neverhuman/bf#8 CLEAN ok=1 \u2026 -> missing: review: no REVIEW: approve 093184dc\u2026 comment`, cross-checked against raw `gh` JSON.\n\nNot checked: the reviewer's vendor (gh exposes logins, not vendors). The TUI's PRs screen consumes this in the next wiring delta.\n\n## Review\nReviewer must be a different vendor (grok, codex or cursor): `REVIEW: approve <head-sha>` via `gh pr review --comment`, then `gh pr merge --rebase --delete-branch`.\n\nbf-author: claude/claude-orch \u00b7 bf-claim: AGENT_CHAT.md 2026-09-18T16:53Z\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
